{"id":"lesson-src-c053fcd172417f","moduleNumber":597,"headword":"alternative","title":"Alternative","subtitle":"替代方案、另一個選擇、代用品——哪些詞真的接近 alternative？","description":"替代方案、另一個選擇、代用品——哪些詞真的接近 alternative？","words":[{"order":1,"word":"Option","meaning":"選項；可選方案","note":"最常見、最自然的近義詞之一。表示可供選擇的一種可能方案。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Taking the train is a cheaper alternative to flying.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"option","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"option","explanation":"最自然的一般可選方案。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"更像功能代用品。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"暗示原本東西被換走。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"只在首選失敗時。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Plan B","explanation":"太口語而且有後備意味。"},{"letter":"F","text":"solution","explanation":"不一定在解決問題。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"We should consider every alternative before making a final decision.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"option","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"option","explanation":"decision 前的可選方案。"},{"letter":"B","text":"choice","explanation":"也很接近，但 every option 更自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"fallback","explanation":"不是所有方案都是後備。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"是偏好。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Online study is an alternative for students who cannot attend in person.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"option","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"option","explanation":"可選學習方式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"稍強調直接取代。"},{"letter":"C","text":"Plan B","explanation":"太口語。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"暗示次選。"},{"letter":"E","text":"decision","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不一定效果相等。"}]}]},{"order":2,"word":"Choice","meaning":"選擇；可選之物","note":"表示可以選擇的人、事物或做法。和 option 很接近，但 choice 也常強調「作出選擇」這個行為本身。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"For short journeys, walking is a healthy alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"choice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"choice","explanation":"日常自然的可選方式。"},{"letter":"B","text":"option","explanation":"也可。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"fallback","explanation":"沒有次選意味。"},{"letter":"F","text":"compromise","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"Students who do not want to take the exam have another alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"choice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"choice","explanation":"自然表示可選方案。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"不是後備語境。"},{"letter":"E","text":"solution","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"是偏好。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"A vegetarian meal is available as an alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"choice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"choice","explanation":"菜單可選項。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"可在特定食材語境中用，但此處不自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fallback","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Plan B","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"variation","explanation":"只是變體。"},{"letter":"F","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不一定等價。"}]}]},{"order":3,"word":"Substitute","meaning":"替代品；代替者","note":"表示可以代替另一樣東西的人或物，重點是功能上取代原本的東西。","example":"這個 alternative 是否是可以直接代替原本東西的「代用品／替代品」？","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"Tofu can be used as an alternative to meat in this recipe.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"substitute","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"substitute","explanation":"功能上代替食材。"},{"letter":"B","text":"option","explanation":"可選但不如 substitute 精確。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"也可能，但食材語境常用 substitute。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Plan B","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"This generic medication is a cheaper alternative to the branded version.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"substitute","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"substitute","explanation":"可直接替代原產品。"},{"letter":"B","text":"choice","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fallback","explanation":"沒有後備意味。"},{"letter":"D","text":"another possibility","explanation":"不夠精確。"},{"letter":"E","text":"decision","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"compromise","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Digital signatures can serve as an alternative to signing documents by hand.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"substitute","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"substitute","explanation":"功能替代。"},{"letter":"B","text":"option","explanation":"也可，但較一般。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fallback","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Plan B","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"variation","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":4,"word":"Replacement","meaning":"替代物；替補；取代品","note":"表示用來取代已不存在、不合適、損壞或被淘汰的人或物。和 substitute 很接近，但更常暗示「原本的東西被換走」。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"We need an alternative for the broken projector before tomorrow's presentation.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"replacement","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"replacement","explanation":"原設備壞掉，需要取代。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"也可能，但 replacement 更自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"option","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"可是後備方案，但不是設備本身的最精準說法。"},{"letter":"E","text":"choice","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"solution","explanation":"太廣。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The club is looking for an alternative for its retiring coach.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"replacement","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"replacement","explanation":"有人離任，需要另一人接替。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"通常更像暫時替補。"},{"letter":"C","text":"option","explanation":"不自然地指人。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Plan B","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"fallback","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"The manufacturer no longer makes this part, so we need an alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"replacement","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"replacement","explanation":"原零件不存在，需要替代零件。"},{"letter":"B","text":"choice","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"C","text":"another possibility","explanation":"不夠具體。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"不是後備方案本身。"},{"letter":"E","text":"compromise","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":5,"word":"Another possibility","meaning":"另一種可能；另一個方案","note":"非常接近 alternative 的描述性說法，適合當有多個可能做法、解釋或方案時。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"One alternative is to hold the meeting online instead.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"another possibility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"another possibility","explanation":"提出另一可行方案。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"若原計劃失敗才更合適。"},{"letter":"E","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"outcome","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"We could repair the machine, but another alternative is to replace it completely.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"another possibility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"another possibility","explanation":"在多個做法中提出另一種。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"是具體替代物，不是完整方案。"},{"letter":"C","text":"choice","explanation":"也可，但 another possibility 更自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Plan B","explanation":"會暗示第一方案失敗後才用。"},{"letter":"E","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"variation","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"If demand remains low, an alternative is to reduce production temporarily.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"another possibility","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"another possibility","explanation":"提出另一個可能做法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"可能，但後備意味更強。"},{"letter":"E","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"decision","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":6,"word":"Other option","meaning":"另一個選項；其他方案","note":"非常接近日常語言中的 alternative。通常用於已有一個方案，再提出別的選項。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If driving is too expensive, the alternative is to take public transport.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"other option","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"other option","explanation":"已有一個方案，再提出另一個。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Plan B","explanation":"會變成後備計劃語氣。"},{"letter":"E","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"solution","explanation":"不一定有問題。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"We can delay the launch; the only alternative is to reduce the number of features.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"other option","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"other option","explanation":"清楚表示另一可選做法。"},{"letter":"B","text":"choice","explanation":"也接近。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fallback","explanation":"若第一方案失敗才更強。"},{"letter":"D","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"variation","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"If the first supplier cannot deliver, what alternative do we have?","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"other option","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"other option","explanation":"日常問「還有甚麼選項」。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"如果問 supplier 本身才可能用。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"decision","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"compromise","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":7,"word":"Different choice","meaning":"不同的選擇","note":"直接表示可以選擇不同的人、物、方法或路線。和 alternative 接近，但較口語、描述性。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If this course is too difficult, you can choose an alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"different choice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different choice","explanation":"不選原本那個，改選另一個。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"fallback","explanation":"沒有次選意味。"},{"letter":"E","text":"Plan B","explanation":"太口語且偏計劃。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"不等於選項。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The menu offers an alternative for customers who do not eat seafood.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"different choice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different choice","explanation":"另一個餐點選擇。"},{"letter":"B","text":"replacement","explanation":"太像替代零件。"},{"letter":"C","text":"fallback","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"another possibility","explanation":"也可，但 choice 更貼近菜單。"},{"letter":"E","text":"decision","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"compromise","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Anyone unhappy with the standard package can select an alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"different choice","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"different choice","explanation":"直接表達改選另一項。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"D","text":"Plan B","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"preference","explanation":"是偏好。"},{"letter":"F","text":"outcome","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":8,"word":"Fallback","meaning":"後備方案；退而求其次的選擇","note":"表示主要方案失敗、不可行或無法使用時，可以改用的後備方案。","example":"這個 alternative 是否只會在首選方案行不通時才使用？","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If the outdoor ceremony is cancelled, the hall is our alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"fallback","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fallback","explanation":"主方案失敗才使用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"option","explanation":"太中性。"},{"letter":"C","text":"choice","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"D","text":"substitute","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"E","text":"replacement","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"F","text":"variation","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"We should have an alternative in case the payment system stops working.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"fallback","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fallback","explanation":"典型 contingency 語境。"},{"letter":"B","text":"other option","explanation":"可用但不突出後備性。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"不一定是物件。"},{"letter":"D","text":"substitute","explanation":"不自然。"},{"letter":"E","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"The team prepared an alternative if the main speaker could not attend.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"fallback","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"fallback","explanation":"首選不能進行時使用。"},{"letter":"B","text":"option","explanation":"也可但較弱。"},{"letter":"C","text":"choice","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"D","text":"substitute","explanation":"如果是替補 speaker 才可，但此句指方案。"},{"letter":"E","text":"solution","explanation":"不一定有問題。"},{"letter":"F","text":"decision","explanation":"不合。"}]}]},{"order":9,"word":"Plan B","meaning":"B 計劃；後備方案","note":"很常見的固定表達，表示原本計劃失敗或不能進行時採用的第二方案。比 fallback 更口語。","example":"","exampleZh":"","exercises":[{"number":1,"original":"If the weather ruins the picnic, we need an alternative.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"Plan B","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Plan B","explanation":"非常自然的口語後備方案。"},{"letter":"B","text":"option","explanation":"太中性。"},{"letter":"C","text":"choice","explanation":"太一般。"},{"letter":"D","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"E","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":2,"original":"The organisers already have an alternative if the venue becomes unavailable.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"Plan B","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Plan B","explanation":"有明確主方案與後備方案。"},{"letter":"B","text":"other option","explanation":"也可但較中性。"},{"letter":"C","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"replacement","explanation":"更像替代物。"},{"letter":"E","text":"preference","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"variation","explanation":"不合。"}]},{"number":3,"original":"Our alternative is to move the event online if travel becomes impossible.","zh":"","upgrade":"","answer":"Plan B","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Plan B","explanation":"明顯是 contingency plan。"},{"letter":"B","text":"substitute","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"C","text":"replacement","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"D","text":"choice","explanation":"可用但不夠有後備感。"},{"letter":"E","text":"equivalent","explanation":"不合。"},{"letter":"F","text":"outcome","explanation":"不合。"}]}]}],"falseSynonyms":[{"word":"Solution","zh":"解決方案不等於所有替代方案 Solution 是用來解決問題的方法；alternative 只表示另一種選擇，不一定解決問題。","point":"We need an alternative to driving. We need a solution to the traffic problem."},{"word":"Decision","zh":"決定不等於選項 Decision 是選擇之後作出的決定；alternative 是作決定之前可供選擇的方案。","point":""},{"word":"Preference","zh":"偏好不等於替代方案 Preference 是你比較喜歡哪一個選項。","point":""},{"word":"Backup","zh":"後備本身不一定是方案 Backup 可以指備份檔案、後備人員、後備設備等；只有在 backup plan / backup option 等語境中才接近 alternative。","point":""},{"word":"Alternative route","zh":"替代路線只是 alternative 的一種具體類型 它是特定應用，不是一般同義詞。","point":""},{"word":"Compromise","zh":"折衷方案不等於另一個選項 Compromise 通常是各方讓步後形成的方案。","point":""},{"word":"Variation","zh":"變體不等於替代選擇 Variation 是同一事物的不同版本，不一定可以代替原方案。","point":""},{"word":"Equivalent","zh":"等價物不等於替代方案 Equivalent 強調價值、功能或效果相等；alternative 不要求完全相等。","point":""}],"sourceFile":"/synonyms/source/alternative_close_synonyms_material.md","priorityRank":597,"omittedExercises":0}